From 6c3d24fb4f233200e486dd73d1ac754cce406f84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junaid Ahamed <junuhammad2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:02:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] overlays: Correct i2c-fan thermal parameter docs

Document the 75000 millicelsius default from the overlay and refer to the midtemp parameter for its lower trip.
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/overlays/README | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/overlays/README
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/overlays/README
@@ -2347,18 +2347,18 @@ Params: addr                    Sets the
                                 parameters - see "dtoverlay -h i2c-bus"
 
         minpwm                  PWM setting for the fan when the SoC is below
-                                mintemp (range 0-255. default 0)
+                                midtemp (range 0-255. default 0)
         maxpwm                  PWM setting for the fan when the SoC is above
                                 maxtemp (range 0-255. default 255)
         midtemp                 Temperature (in millicelsius) at which the fan
                                 begins to speed up (default 50000)
 
         midtemp_hyst            Temperature delta (in millicelsius) below
-                                mintemp at which the fan will drop to minrpm
+                                midtemp at which the fan will drop to minrpm
                                 (default 2000)
 
         maxtemp                 Temperature (in millicelsius) at which the fan
-                                will be held at maxrpm (default 70000)
+                                will be held at maxrpm (default 75000)
 
         maxtemp_hyst            Temperature delta (in millicelsius) below
                                 maxtemp at which the fan begins to slow down
